Lua calls are very slow and can't be something that executes tens or hundreds of times each frame.
I very much believe the following Lua code in `Tile.lua` needs to be eliminated:
```
function MovementCost_Standard ( tile )
if (tile.furniture == nil) then
return tile.Type.BaseMovementCost
end
return tile.Type.BaseMovementCost * tile.furniture.movementCost
end
```
If a mod wants to modify movement costs, they should do see by setting a parameter, which then gets read by the C# movement cost function.
