Unity documentation says:
Windows Store Apps: On Universal Windows 10 Apps the touch screen keyboard is only supported in XAML based applications with touch input support.
My app is with Build Type D3D and not xaml so this is the first strange thing.
However since the keyboard is shown we can try to disable the touch input support.
To do this we can define a new BaseInput used by the BaseInputModule where touchSupported is overrided and setted to false.
BaseInputModule has a protected property m_InputOverride that we can use to tell unity to use the new BaseInput.
That said, as a temporary workaround, I made the attached script that can be added to the EventSystem game object of the scene or to another game object (in the latter case you must set the field BaseInputModule with the current input module).
In my case it seems to work (the native keyboard is not shown).
