Hi Stephen,
I am sorry but I don't understand if your fix is also for HMD and where to check if the keyboard is opaque.
However I have seen that the keyboard already uses a custom InputField (SliderInputField).
If we make an override of LateUpdate like this:
` protected override void LateUpdate()
{
base.LateUpdate();
if (m_Keyboard != null )
{
m_Keyboard.active = false;
m_Keyboard = null;
}
}
`
the problem seems fixed (no second keyboard appear and no exception is thrown).
LateUpdate calls ActivateInputFieldInternal and opens the keyboard.
The script is no more necessary.
In my case I see that the keyboard is not null only one time
Tested with Unity 2017.3.1p1 and HMD.
