I found a less-than-perfect workaround: set KeyboardInputField 's interactable bool to false. This will prevent the OS keyboard from showing up, and upon user click, it brings up only the MRToolKit keyboard. However, this comes at a price... you would lose access to the interactable features of the InputField UI, such as highlighting selection and a blinking caret...
Like Mark mentioned, this also needs to be done for the InputField within the Keyboard.prefab itself. In addition, I recommend changing the Disabled colour to white and adding the following script into SliderInputField.cs to set caret position at the end upon user click:
public override void OnPointerClick(PointerEventData eventData)
{
base.OnPointerClick(eventData);
MoveTextEnd(false);
}

