Hi @jbaessens, we were able to reproduce the issue from our side. It seems, the issue is caused by `managed code stripping`, although set to `low`, it's stripping some part of the ably reflection code. Can you add `link.xml` file under `Assets` with the following content? We have tested the change and seems to be working for us. It will make sure, no part of `ably.dll` is stripped during IL2CPP build.
```
<linker>
<assembly fullname="IO.Ably" preserve="all" />
</linker>
```
We have created an active issue to include it as a part of Unity Package
https://github.com/ably/ably-dotnet/issues/1113

