Nice find! It looks like you correctly identified the bug. I think what we could do is make an a separate nlopt_func definition that anticipates that being null. In other words, add this definition:
```csharp
[UnmanagedFunctionPointer(CallingConvention.Cdecl)]
private delegate double nlopt_func_nograd(uint n, [MarshalAs(UnmanagedType.LPArray, SizeParamIndex = 0), In] double[] x, IntPtr gradient, IntPtr data);
```
Then modify `SetMinObjective` (the one that doesn't expose the gradient) to this:
```csharp
public void SetMinObjective(Func<double[], double> objective)
{
nlopt_func_nograd func = (u, values, gradient, data) => objective.Invoke(values);
...
```
We would also change the func type in `AddLessOrEqualZeroConstraint` and verify that `gradient == IntPtr.Zero` there. The `_funcCache` exists just to keep the functions from the GC. Its value type could change to `object`, and that would still achieve the necessary purpose there.
